#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Read-only planner for migrating a Dish Asana project's task sections.

Purpose
-------
Reuse the mature evidence/reconciliation logic from refresh_dish_desk.py, but
produce a migration ledger instead of an operator dashboard.

This script NEVER mutates Asana or GitHub. It defaults to the Development
Workflow project, while accepting another exact project GID so the same
evidence pipeline can be reused for later project migrations.

Outputs
-------
- dish-asana-migration-<project-gid>.json
- dish-asana-migration-<project-gid>.csv

For every task in the selected project, it records:
- current task/project/section state
- durable priority evidence
- GitHub PR / lifecycle evidence where present
- proposed target section
- proposed stable title
- proposed coarse Code Area
- confidence and reasons
- migration blockers / human-review flags

Migration policy encoded here
-----------------------------
Target sections:
  Needs Processing
  Needs Research
  Needs Agentic Review
  Needs Human Review
  Waiting on Dependency
  Ready
  Under Development
  Done

Important rules:
- preserve project/task identity;
- title text is evidence for cleanup, not lifecycle/priority authority;
- priority is never inferred from audit severity or lifecycle words in titles;
- handoff sent != Under Development;
- GitHub/lifecycle owns detailed execution state once development starts;
- source merge alone != Done when residual rollout/operator/runtime work remains;
- ambiguous raw findings prefer Needs Processing rather than guessed Research/Ready;
- deterministic output is a proposal/validation surface, not a replacement for
  semantic reconciliation when evidence conflicts.
"""

import argparse
import csv
import datetime
import json
import os
